<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;I&gt;&amp;gt; What is the lvalues here?&lt;/I&gt;&lt;P&gt;

($x, $y, $z) are after the first assignment ready for the second one.&lt;P&gt;

Lvalue means left value of assignment (the recipient)&lt;P&gt;


See also [DOC://perlglossary|&lt;tt&gt;perlglossary&lt;/tt&gt;]
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt; &lt;I&gt;lvalue&lt;/I&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;I&gt;Term used by language lawyers for a storage location you can assign a new value to, such as a variable or an element of an array. The “l” is short for “left”, as in the left side of an assignment, a typical place for lvalues. An lvaluable function or expression is one to which a value may be assigned, as in pos($x) = 10 .&lt;/I&gt;
&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;P&gt;

